package CanvasNet {
    part def ExpressionFunctions {
        doc /* The internal static partial ExpressionFunctions with the ExpressionFunction delegate, the ExpressionFunctionContext, and the ExpressionRegex class: the closed table of the 57 whitelisted pure functions that an expression may call (abs, acos, acosh, asin, asinh, atan, atan2, atanh, ceil, clamp, cos, cosh, exp, floor, log, log10, max, min, pow, round, sign, sin, sinh, sqrt, tan, tanh, trunc; lower, upper, trim, substring, slice, indexof, lastindexof, startswith, endswith, includes, replace, split, join, pad, length; isArray, isBoolean, isDate, isFinite, isNaN, isNumber, isObject, isRegExp, isString, isValid, toBoolean, toNumber, toString; regexp, test), with Names, TryGet, and Invoke (an unknown name is an ArgumentException) and no random, clock, reflection, file, or network function. The functions follow JavaScript and Vega results independently of the culture (negative zero kept, isNaN and isFinite not coercing, toBoolean, toNumber, and toString giving null for null and the empty string, pad aligned as in Vega), results are bounded by MaxStringLength, and the host math library is used for the transcendental functions. The ExpressionFunctionContext is the per-evaluation context that counts the steps (Step, and ChargeSize for one step per 64 characters or elements of size-proportional work), polls the cancellation token, enforces the string limit, and caches at most 64 regular expressions; ExpressionRegex translates a JavaScript pattern (the flags g, i, m, s, and u; at most 1,024 characters; \d, \w, and $ semantics adjusted) into a .NET Regex that uses RegexOptions.NonBacktracking with the invariant culture (a 5 second backstop timeout) and falls back for the patterns that engine rejects (look-around, back-references) to the backtracking engine with a 100 millisecond timeout that fails closed, an invalid or over-long pattern being a located VegaLiteRenderException. Date and time, format, color, geographic, scale, dataflow, and statistical functions are deferred and are reported by the FeatureCatalog. */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Expressions/ExpressionFunctions.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Expressions/ExpressionFunctions.Text.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Expressions/ExpressionFunctions.Types.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Expressions/ExpressionFunctions.Regex.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Expressions/ExpressionFunctionContext.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Expressions/ExpressionRegex.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Expressions/ExpressionFunctionsTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-vega-lite/expressions/expression-functions.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-vega-lite/expressions/expression-functions.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-vega-lite/expressions/expression-functions.yaml */
    }
}
